new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e2c6efc
--- /dev/null
+++ b/CHANGES-3.6.0.md
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+# TickTrade Intelligence Core 3.6.0
+
+Changes since 3.5.0 (the version you were running):
+
+## Code ZIP uploads
+- ZIPs made from a working folder now import. Dependency, build and version-control folders
+  (`node_modules`, `dist`, `build`, `.git`, ...) are ignored before any limit is applied instead of
+  making the whole upload fail with "invalid or has too many entries".
+- ZIPs made with the Finder (containing `__MACOSX`, `.DS_Store` and `._` files) import like a clean
+  export; the real top folder is still stripped.
+- Error messages say what is wrong and what to do: unreadable/corrupt archive, too many files
+  (with the count), too large (with the size), instead of one generic message.
+- The upload report lists the ignored folders and how many files each held.
+
+## Diagnostics
+- Every unexpected error is now written with its traceback to `data/logs/errors.log`
+  (secrets redacted, rotated at 2 MB). Messages in the app name the error type and point to the log.
+  This covers HTTP requests, code ZIP imports, document imports, Studio publication/rollback,
+  engineering tasks and runtime (Docker) jobs.
+
+## Studio
+- Patch limits raised from 200 KB per file / 1 MB total to 2 MB per file / 4 MB total, so large
+  files such as `apps/engine/src/npc/npc-simulator.service.ts` (702 KB) can now be changed.
+
+## Launcher
+- `Start TickTrade.command` prefers Homebrew Python 3.13/3.12/3.11 and prints which interpreter
+  and which address it uses.
diff --git a/ENGINEERING_API.md b/ENGINEERING_API.md
index c9fcdbf..6ad693e 100644
--- a/ENGINEERING_API.md
+++ b/ENGINEERING_API.md
@@ -80,7 +80,7 @@ Patch candidate:
 {"snapshot_id":"snap-<id>","changes":[{"path":"calculator.py","before_sha256":"<current file SHA-256>","content":"def add(a, b):\n    return a + b\n"}]}
 ```
 
-For a new file, `before_sha256` must be null. Candidate creation does not execute the patch, install dependencies or touch the original repo. Changes are capped at 20 files, 200 KB per file and 1 MB total; path, secret-pattern, stale-hash and no-op checks apply.
+For a new file, `before_sha256` must be null. Candidate creation does not execute the patch, install dependencies or touch the original repo. Changes are capped at 20 files, 2 MB per file and 4 MB total; path, secret-pattern, stale-hash and no-op checks apply.
 
 ## Persistence and trust
 
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 91a1d1d..7503c9f 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -20,7 +20,7 @@ Open **Find & fix issues → Development studio** or **Improve TickTrade → Dev
 
 Choose **Generate handoff**, then **Copy** or **Download brief**. The pack contains your owner instructions, acceptance criteria, attached reference excerpts, exact repository/snapshot IDs and mapped file hashes. Export the matching working ZIP when the recipient needs source files. Nothing is sent externally by these controls.
 
-Paste or load the returned JSON under **Returned JSON changes**, then choose **Create candidate from JSON**. It must identify the exact repository and snapshot. Existing files may use complete `content` or 1–20 exact `edits: [{old, new}]`; each old string must match exactly once at the corresponding step. New files require complete content and a null `before_sha256`. The limits are 20 changed files, 200 KB per expanded source file, 1 MB per lockfile and 1 MB overall. Server validation checks original hashes, paths, matches, expanded file sizes and recognizable credentials. Importing creates a candidate; review and application are separate steps.
+Paste or load the returned JSON under **Returned JSON changes**, then choose **Create candidate from JSON**. It must identify the exact repository and snapshot. Existing files may use complete `content` or 1–20 exact `edits: [{old, new}]`; each old string must match exactly once at the corresponding step. New files require complete content and a null `before_sha256`. The limits are 20 changed files, 2 MB per expanded source file, 4 MB per lockfile and 4 MB overall. Server validation checks original hashes, paths, matches, expanded file sizes and recognizable credentials. Importing creates a candidate; review and application are separate steps.
 
 For optional Astra cloud work, open **Setup & sources → AI model & hardware**, choose OpenAI with `gpt-6-astra`, supply your own API key and explicitly allow cloud requests. This is an OpenAI API configuration, not an automatic connection to a Codex account. Keep credentials out of briefs and handoff files.
 
diff --git a/Start TickTrade.command b/Start TickTrade.command
index 3c0dcff..17b1eb3 100755
--- a/Start TickTrade.command	
+++ b/Start TickTrade.command	
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@
 set -eu
 cd -- "${0:A:h}"
